@nsobid-592C7051A4E620563D0296096D8F0AC5

# Splatoon 2 5.5.2 - 3840x2160 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces the render/scan-buffer resolution to 3840x2160 (native 1920x1080).
// Patches Cstm::SysInit::getScanBufferSize (the packed WxH scan-buffer constant).
// MEMORY: total heap arrangement ~3278 MB, which exceeds the ~2.9 GiB the default
// 4 GiB DRAM Size gives the game. Set Ryujinx > System > DRAM Size to 6 GiB or
// higher (6 / 8 / 12 GiB) before launching, or boot aborts while creating the
// graphics heap.

@enabled
003A7394 09E081D2
003A7398 090EC1F2
// Defeat the dynamic-resolution controller (Cmn::GPUPerfController). It reads the
// scan-buffer size every frame and then clamps the presented image two ways:
// updateFrameBufferScale_ scales the framebuffer down, and calc() pins
// sead::GraphicsNvn::setDisplayBufferWindowCrop to an ABSOLUTE height from its
// resolution ladder (1080p) -- so without this the render target scales but the
// image handed to the display stays 1920x1080. Both paths are already skipped when
// the controller's own full-resolution flag (+0xE8) is set, so force its three reads
// to 1 (LDRB W8,[X19,#0xE8] -> MOVZ W8,#1) and the game takes its own full-res path.
001157B4 28008052
0011580C 28008052
0011592C 28008052
// Enlarge the fixed dynamic-texture GPU pool so Depth-of-Field / post-effect
// buffers fit at this resolution (Cmn::GfxMgr::getDynamicTextureAllocatorMemSize, 128 MB -> 512 MB).
// Without this the game aborts in agl::utl::DynamicTextureAllocator::alloc_ (pool exhausted).
0010BADC 0000A452
// Enlarge the graphics heap partition (Cstm heap arrangement mGfxSize) so the bigger
// dynamic-texture pool above can actually be carved from it (220 MB -> 896 MB). Without this the
// game aborts at boot in agl::Initialize -> DynamicTextureAllocator::initialize (heap too small).
0039C564 0A00A752
// Enlarge the system heap partition (Cstm heap arrangement mSysSize, 200 MB -> 512 MB).
// Every Lp/Cmn manager task carves its heap out of whatever is left of this heap, so
// once the higher resolution eats into it the tasks created last get nothing -- seen on
// the March builds as "heap create failed. [Coconut]" in Cmn::CoconutMgr::prepare.
0039C560 0900A452
@stop

// Resolution/LOD technique derived from Fl4sh9174's retail Splatoon 2 5.5.x mods.
// Remaining offsets reverse-engineered against the Cstm/Lp + gsys/agl engine; 5.5.2
// is symbol-stripped, so every site here was matched by signature and byte-verified.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
